From: "Pluet, LLC" <358065800+pluetllc@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ao_spatial: the rendered 7.1.4 as lossless linear PCM over
 HDMI, and Force Dolby MAT for decoded multichannel PCM

The spatial output rendered TrueHD Atmos and DTS:X objects to 7.1.4 and
always encoded that as APAC, a lossy codec (49 dB signal-to-error against the
render on a TrueHD Atmos film excerpt), before tvOS decoded it again and sent
Dolby MAT. With SpatialAudioBridge patch 0001 the renderer can enqueue the
rendered feeds as 32-bit float linear PCM in Apple's Atmos 7.1.4 layout
instead, bit for bit, beside the same Atmos activator.

--ao-spatial-output=auto|apac|lpcm picks it. auto (the default) sends linear
PCM where the audio session's route is HDMI, the receiver or soundbar the
lossless MAT path is for, and APAC everywhere else (AirPlay, headphones,
built-in speakers), where the system spatializes APAC. If the renderer turns
linear PCM down (its status fails, or AVFoundation reports an error), the
output reloads with APAC and keeps to it for this player
(MP_SPATIAL_OUTPUT_FAILED, mpv_global.spatial_lpcm_failed); a stream
without objects still falls back to decoding as before.

--ao-spatial-force-mat (default no) also takes decoded PCM of more than two
channels: bed-only TrueHD, DTS-HD MA without DTS:X, multichannel PCM, and
anything else mpv decodes to 5.1 or more. The output offers only the 7.1.4
speakers (mpv remaps or downmixes nothing else), asks for float at 48 kHz
(the Apple TV's output rate), places each channel unchanged in its 7.1.4
slot (a 5.1 with back surrounds at the sides, as Apple's 5.1 has them) and
plays it through the same lossless renderer and activator, so tvOS sends
Dolby MAT instead of multichannel PCM. mpv's own volume already applies to
decoded PCM, so the renderer stays at unity there. Stereo and every
bitstream but TrueHD and DTS-HD (AC-3, E-AC-3) go to the next output as
before.

The spatial-audio-output property says what the output sends: "apac",
"lpcm" or "pcm" (Force Dolby MAT), unavailable otherwise; it changes with
the audio reconfig event, like current-ao.

---
diff --git a/audio/out/ao_spatial.h b/audio/out/ao_spatial.h
index e9d11c0..5f7c106 100644
--- a/audio/out/ao_spatial.h
+++ b/audio/out/ao_spatial.h
@@ -10,9 +10,30 @@ enum {
     MP_SPATIAL_DISCONTINUITY,
     // The stream cannot be rendered; fall back to PCM.
     MP_SPATIAL_FAILED,
+    // The renderer turned down linear PCM: open again with APAC, or leave
+    // decoded PCM to the next output.
+    MP_SPATIAL_OUTPUT_FAILED,
 };
 
-void *mp_spatial_create(int codec, void *synchronizer, size_t buffer_limit);
+// What the output sends the system (the spatial-audio-output property).
+enum {
+    MP_SPATIAL_KIND_NONE,
+    // TrueHD Atmos or DTS:X rendered to 7.1.4 and encoded as APAC.
+    MP_SPATIAL_KIND_APAC,
+    // Rendered to 7.1.4 and sent as 32-bit float linear PCM: lossless.
+    MP_SPATIAL_KIND_LPCM,
+    // Decoded PCM sent as linear PCM next to the Atmos activator (Force
+    // Dolby MAT): lossless.
+    MP_SPATIAL_KIND_PCM,
+};
+
+// codec: 1 TrueHD, 2 DTS-HD. lossless: linear PCM instead of APAC.
+void *mp_spatial_create(int codec, bool lossless, void *synchronizer, size_t buffer_limit);
+// Interleaved float PCM at 48 kHz with `channels` channels; slots[i] is
+// channel i's place in Apple's Atmos 7.1.4 order (L R C LFE Ls Rs Rls Rrs Vhl
+// Vhr Ltr Rtr), or -1 to drop it.
+void *mp_spatial_create_pcm(const int8_t *slots, int channels, void *synchronizer,
+                            size_t buffer_limit);
 void mp_spatial_destroy(void *output);
 void mp_spatial_begin(void *output, int64_t nanoseconds);
 size_t mp_spatial_write(void *output, const void *bytes, size_t size);
